ood  diary episodes I have watched to date  she's not trying to sell us on a  celebrity diet full of green juices and  kale salads or smoothies from erwan or  extravagant meals made with specialty  ingredients she does what she can with  what she has on hand and the time that's  available to her and she isn't afraid to  take shortcuts and call on her family  members for support we eat dinner all as  a family oh we order out from everywhere  I love to order food that I don't make  for instance I don't make sushi I will  order out sushi I don't do Thai I will  order out Thai I don't do Indian I will  order out Indian we just did just get a  pizza oven so we made our own pizzas for  the first time my daughter puts  pineapple on olives cheese and tomato  sauce my son likes tomato sauce and a  very light amount of cheese my husband  does mushrooms jalapenos and olives on  his cheese tomato sauce DIY pizza is a  great family meal that allows kids to  get involved in the kitchen the more  autonomy they have over choices like  toppings the more like likely they are  to try it and you're not short order  cooking to each kid's unique meal  preferences everyone has the same meal  they just kind of get to choose what  goes on it oh my beverage of choice it's  water because it's healthy for you my  honest beverage of choice is a glass of  wine relatable but the whole family now  loves Poppy  okay poppy beverages anybody here poppy  lollipop I feel like it's because it  says Prebiotic and micro clearly this is  this is healthy I don't know if it is or  isn't but boy do I like a nice little  puppy first off if she likes poppy  regardless of the health claims then  that is reason enough to continue to  enjoy it as for the Prebiotic claims  poppy beverages get their Prebiotic  Boost from apple cider vinegar which  contains the Prebiotic pectin which is  naturally found in a variety of fruits  including apples but one we don't  actually know how much apple cider  vinegar is in this drink probably not a  lot of it or it would just taste like  straight up vinegar and two you can  actually obtain far more Prebiotic  pectin from eating a single Apple than  you can from drinking a tablespoon of  apple cider vinegar but again if Mila  and the whole family love poppy then by  all means just keep enjoying it but at  the end of the day you're better off  getting your Prebiotic thicks from some  fruits and veg after dinner the children  are always they're always allowed like  to have a bite of something sweet and  then my husband and I open the freezer  and have ice cream every night oh girl  what kind of ice cream we have so much  ice cream people know I love ice cream  and so for my birthday they send me like  ice cream of the month clubs or like  some sort of variety we have so much we  always have ice cream I love ice cream  my kids love ice cream  um my husband loves ice cream it's my  favorite food group we have eaten at I  would say every ice cream place in Los  Angeles I swear this woman is my soul  mate and again having a nighttime ice  cream ritual with your hubby especially  when that hubby is Ashton Kutcher is  Major couples goals because I too always  have a ton of ice cream in the house so  I love this little tidbit overall I  think this is one of the most relatable  food Dyers episodes I've ever watched it  wasn't overly curated or trying to  promote an unattainable celebrity  lifestyle I mean Mila really just kept  it super real and wasn't afraid to say  hey I'm a busy working mom who is doing  my best to feed my family and myself  sometimes that means eating like scraps  off of my family's plate so please let  this serve as a reminder to all the  working parents out there who feel like  they need to do it all or feel like they  are always failing it is absolutely okay  to lean on kitchen Time Savers or ask  for support from family and friends for  most of us it's not realistic to prepare  every meal from scratch while also  raising a family and working full-time  and I think Mila is a great example of a  super mom who has found a way to do the  things that bring her Joy without  putting too much pressure on herself to  do them perfectly and on that note  that's all that I have for you guys  today if you like this video please give  it the thumbs up leave me a comment  below on who or what he'd like to see me  review next subscribe to this Channel  and I'll see you next time on Abby's  kitchen bye  [Music]
 

